.TH PTRACE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
ptrace \- invokes linux ptrace with four fixed arguments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/ptrace.h>
.B long ptrace(long request, pid_t process, void* address, void* data);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes Linux ptrace with four fixed arguments. Unlike libc ptrace, PEEK requests write the word through data and return zero; data must be a writable long pointer.
For requests requiring integer data, use
.BR ptrace_value (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ptrace (2)
